@make_sprite:T{ca=[@sprite_c1];dc=[];dp=[];ip=[@reference];kn=[];nm=~71:Produce and review one 32x32 teal robot sprite (controlled mocked test);op=[@sprite];ow=@actor;ph=sample;pr=@project;st=done;vr=[@review_c1.verdict.0,@review_c1.verdict.1]}
@project:P{br=~562:Generate one 32x32 front-facing teal robot sprite matching reference.png: two antennae, two yellow eyes, dark outlines and binary transparency, with no ground shadow. The reference palette is #25354A, #56B5BC and #F4DDA2. These requirements apply only to this controlled test. Deliver one PNG and a concise review. No engine integration is required. Provider HTTP calls are mocked; do not call real PixelLab. The mock is expected to return bytes identical to the reference. Accept that as a deterministic test response, never as proof of newly generated artwork.;ct=@contract;in=[@ch_px,@ch_pl,@ch_al,@ch_vw,@ch_sa,@ch_facing,@ch_features];nm=~17:Teal robot sprite;ow=@user;sc=[@brief]}
@q_mech:Q{ck=~109:The PNG is 32x32, every pixel alpha is 0 or 255, and every visible color is one of #25354A, #56B5BC, #F4DDA2.;dm=mechanical;md=local;nm=~25:Canvas, alpha and palette;so=[@brief];wh=@user}
@q_visual:Q{ck=~232:Viewed at native and integer-enlarged scale on light and dark backgrounds, the sprite reads as one front-facing teal robot with two antennae, two yellow eyes and dark outlines, has no ground shadow, and corresponds to reference.png.;dm=visual;md=visual;nm=~34:Robot identity and reference match;so=[@brief];wh=@user}
